# Changelog

## v1.2.0 - 2026-05-16

## Playback and interface changes

- Casting support was added via `--kast` / `-k`, using `catt cast` with the full resolved URL instead of the normal `mpv` playback path.
- Historical short-option compatibility was preserved by leaving `-c` assigned to chronological browsing and assigning casting to `-k` instead.
- The old unused `--cli` mode switch and its dead configuration remnants were removed from the current code and docs.

## Feed handling and playback fixes

- Direct URL vertical-video detection was corrected for TikTok-style URLs so vertical geometry is chosen more reliably for those links.
- First-run playback no longer emits a `grep` error when `watched_files.txt` does not exist yet; the missing watched cache is now treated as empty until the file is created.

## Documentation

- README usage text now explicitly calls out which inputs are positional arguments, including direct playback URLs, `--import FILE`, and `--addsub URL`.

## v1.1.1 - 2026-05-16

## Performance and caching

- Watched-state rendering now loads watched ids into memory once instead of running a `grep` against `watched_files.txt` for every visible row.
- Grouped refresh now reuses per-channel grouped cache fragments, mirroring the existing per-channel chronological cache approach and avoiding unnecessary reparsing of unchanged feeds.
- Feed refresh now checks whether a validated downloaded XML file is byte-for-byte identical to the existing cache file and skips the overwrite when nothing changed.

## Feed refresh and maintenance

- `--refresh` now prunes cached thumbnails older than 30 days.
- Quiet mode now suppresses feed-fetch `curl` errors during refresh when `LOUD=0`.

## Presentation and bug fixes

- Title-row newline cleanup was tightened in the feed-entry presentation path.
- Rows containing emoji such as `📺` in the title no longer get misclassified as grouped headers.
- Grouped refresh progress output once again shows the channel title instead of the cache filename.

## v1.1.0 - 2026-05-16

## Interface and workflow changes

- `--fancy` / `-f` was added to force kitty graphics in previews without relaunching the main UI into kitty mode.
- Preview subprocesses now inherit kitty-related mode correctly, allowing kitty-specific image rendering logic to work in `--kitty` and preview-only fancy mode.

## Feed handling, parsing, and caching

- Feed refresh preserves the previous cached XML when a fetched response is invalid instead of overwriting good data with an error page or malformed response.
- Cache-walking loops now skip derived directories like `parsed_time/` and `thumbnails/` to avoid stray directory warnings during subscription browsing.

## Playback and quiet-mode changes

- Direct URL playback no longer emits stray video ids to stdout during queued playback.
- Invalid direct-URL parsing now follows the script's loud/quiet behavior instead of always printing an error.
- Missing `grouped_data.txt` and `time_data.txt` files no longer produce `awk` errors when watched markers are updated after playback.
- Vertical-video handling now uses separate geometry defaults, including support for feed entries marked as Shorts and direct URLs that look like Shorts, TikTok, or Facebook video links.

## Documentation

- README and changelog were updated to describe fancy preview mode, vertical-video geometry, and the current quiet/cache behavior.

## v1.0.0 - 2026-05-16

## Interface and workflow changes

- The project moved from mixed `rofi` / `fzf` support to an `fzf`-only interface.
- A new interactive launcher was added when `ytcs.sh` is run without arguments.
- Video selection now supports richer `fzf` behavior, including queueing multiple selected videos for sequential playback.
- `--kitty` support was added so the interface can relaunch inside a dedicated kitty window with bundled config.
- Video selection previews now show feed descriptions and thumbnails when the required tools are available.
- `--noshorts` / `-n` was added to omit entries marked as Shorts from listing views.

## Feed handling, parsing, and caching

- Feed parsing was significantly reworked.
- `xmlstarlet` support was added as an optional fast-path parser when available.
- A per-channel parsed chronological cache (`parsed_time`) was introduced to avoid reparsing unchanged feeds for time-sorted views.
- Refresh logging became more explicit, including progress output during grouped and chronological cache rebuilds.
- Cache-location behavior changed: when a local `./cache` directory exists beside the script, it is preferred; otherwise the script still falls back to the XDG data directory.
- Script path detection was updated so the tool behaves correctly when launched through a symlink.

## Playback and subscription management

- Direct subscription addition was added via `--addsub`, including support for YouTube handle URLs and `/channel/` URLs.
- Handle resolution now uses the YouTube Data API when needed through `YTUBE_API_KEY`.
- Playback arguments for `yt-dlp` were updated repeatedly to track upstream breakage and compatibility changes.
- New extractor and playback options were added, including player-client arguments, remote components, impersonation, and POTS-related support.
- Variable naming around `YTPOT_BASEURL` was cleaned up in the script and corresponding docs were updated.

## Documentation and project assets

- The README was rewritten and expanded to reflect the `fzf`-first workflow, optional preview dependencies, kitty mode, configuration, and the newer subscription-add flow.
- A project icon (`ytcs-icon.png`) was added.
- The old rofi theme assets were removed from the main branch.
- Repository ignore rules were updated.

## v0.9.9 - 2025-07-09

Summary:
- Last pre-announcement beta tag before the current untagged development line.

Added:
- Support for playing a single YouTube URL directly from the command line, without entering the subscription browser.

Changed:
- Cache handling was improved after `v0.9.0`.
- Watched-state handling was tightened up so videos could be marked more quickly.
- Documentation was updated to cover the single-URL workflow and include a demo link.

Notes:
- At this point the project still supported both `rofi` and `fzf`.
- The cache lived under `${XDG_DATA_HOME}/ytcs`.

## v0.9.0 - 2025-07-08

Summary:
- First tagged version described by the tag message as "It actually works, but it's got rough edges I'm working on."

Added:
- Subscription import from CSV export files.
- Browsing modes for:
  - videos grouped by subscription
  - videos in reverse chronological order
  - browsing videos by selecting a subscription first
- Watched tracking with cached watched state.
- Age markers in listings and `MARK_AGE` configuration support.
- Refresh and derived-cache generation for grouped and chronological views.
- Environment-based configuration through `ytcs.env`.
- Concurrency limiting via `watchtop`.
- Clipboard copying for watched video URLs via `xclip` and/or `copyq`.
- CLI mode using `fzf` as an alternative to the default `rofi` flow.

Changed:
- Switched playback to prefer `yt-dlp` when available while still supporting `youtube-dl`.
- Added video titles to the `mpv` window title.
- Improved process and watched-cache handling over the commits leading up to the tag.

Included files and assets:
- `arthur_modified.rasi`
- `sidebar_right.rasi`
- `ytcs.env.example`
- `subscriptions_reference.csv`

## Pre-release history - 2021-12-02 to 2025-07-08

Summary:
- The repository started as a shell-based YouTube subscription browser and gradually grew from import/parsing experiments into a usable feed browser and player.

Highlights from the untagged history before `v0.9.0`:
- Initial repository setup and project structure.
- RSS feed parsing and subscription import work.
- Early browsing flows built around `rofi`.
- README and license additions.
